# ZON-05 factual Original direct-member review proposal

This immutable Source proposal adapts the accepted RAD03 factual review stage.
It does not execute a target, solve a moisture balance, compare numerical
answers or update gates. Root and another author must review it before use.
Native01, the reviewed ZON05 freezer and strict PE reader are literal pins.
All future actual execution/build/scope/result identities remain runtime
path#SHA operands, not values invented in this proposal.

The existing ten required options remain: approved-source-sha256,
native-execution, results, freeze-receipt, freeze-execution, build,
build-execution, build-review, build-review-execution and output-dir. With the
usual python -X utf8 -B reader prefix, this is argc25. --results must identify
the genuine Native recorder stdout itself with explicit SHA. Native argv is
exactly the actual derived executable and the actual frozen request (argc2).
There is no helper result-file name, self-reported binary digest, admission
digest, contract digest or synthetic per-case error file obligation.

The frozen request is a byte-exact copy of the accepted five-key fixture,
including 21 declared cases and 43 ordered member requests. Native does not
consume sidecars. QA joins their actual freeze/admission/projection/contracts,
literal policy, current ZON-05 amendment/check and current document identities
through the real recorder and reviewed writer. Historical metadata in held
source inventories is not rebound as the live plan. No old plan SHA is a
current-document requirement. Current scope role is real-ZON-05-check-only;
inventory key is zon05_policy_source_inventory. The actual before archives and
current after-documents come from that amendment. Build freezes refer to this
same packet; full freezer and compact strict PE stdout are authenticated.

The build must prove actual restored717 registrations plus three authentic
inherited RAD registrations and one new ZON registration, with only one fresh
ZON compilation, four admitted Native sources and the genuine unchanged
core ZoneSpaceHeatBalanceData::correctHumRat provider. Core counts are
643/631/12 and protected count52. The approved PE review independently
inspects both actual files and compares their retained runtime maps. This
reader authenticates that metadata without reading or hashing binary payloads.

shape.review(result, request, need) returns (counts, integrity). It validates
every actual case and ordered invoked prefix, exact literal input custody,
all18 scalar and six four-slot zone fields, 12 moisture source owners, full
allocated node/inlet bounds/order, actual clock/route flags and psychrometric
owners. Prepared input bits match the supplied fixture tokens. Non-feedback
nodes and current/average/history/other zone fields retain actual own bits.
Only temporary W, the actual positive feedback node W/H and genuine
psychrometric state may change. No expected temporary W or enthalpy is computed.

Scalar DTO checks decode copied binary64 representation solely to validate
decimal/class/bit serialization, including signed zero and null nonfinite
decimals. The literal four profile policy is inherited unchanged; QA never
uses those tolerances to compare answers. Cache rows retain actual original
indices/tags/values and nondefault predicate; no hash, HIT, Psat or local helper
call outcome is reconstructed. The actual full cache capacity and error indices
are observed owners, not defaults supplied by the reader.

Actual Native diagnostic indices/level/text and error stream stay Native-only
context. Their ordered per-operation windows must cover the actual retained
message ledger. No causal warning category or Rust global backend parity is
claimed. Unobserved A/B/C/rho/Hg/Wsat and guard decisions remain unobserved;
history selection/current/average commit and parser/production remain uninvoked.

Counts are derived from records only: cases, correctHumRat, source_returns,
caught_source_exceptions, declared_unreached_operations, snapshots,
scalar_DTO_visits and source_messages. Complete case coverage with a caught
exception retains its actual stopped prefix/counts and integrity failure.
The case's missing suffix is declared unreached and cannot become success.
A malformed/incomplete/absent stdout ledger instead has unknown actual counts,
complete_requested_record_ledger_validated:false and no baseline release.
Genuine OS launch failure may retain exit:null only with nonempty launch_error;
all successful predecessor receipts retain the existing strict integer0 rule.
Nonzero process status, caught source stop, malformed records, unavailable
records or process/status disagreement always prevent Rust_baseline_released.

Report schema is zon05-independent-original-data-review.v1. Status is
pass-actual-original-data-and-provenance-before-Rust only for genuine process0,
complete requested ledger and no integrity failures; otherwise it is
fail-original-process-or-observation-integrity-before-Rust. Direct refs remain
reviewed_results/native_execution/request/native_admission_contract/projection/
contracts/build/build_execution/build_review/build_review_execution, actual
packet freeze/execution and actual scope amendment/check. Full report stdout
and three executed_reader_sources archives bind the exact source bytes.
numerical_PASS_claimed remains false, comparison/mismatch counts remain null,
and history/production/full-card gates remain unclaimed.

IO retains the exact RAD functions with only the card directory changed.
Source/input files keep the existing 64,000,000-byte physical guard and parsed
JSON keeps the 16,000,000-byte guard; no policy is tuned from actual output.
The three RAD before sources/docs and three exact generated diffs are retained.
Only stdlib AST/hash/diff metadata checks are performed at authoring time;
reviewed sources are not imported, executed, formatted or tested.

